# netsurf: download progress -- a progress strip, rate and time left, and
# a Downloads page with cancel (patch 245; roadmap WS-E)
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 243)
#
# A download showed "downloading x: 42% (120 KiB)" in the message box in
# the middle of the screen for its whole length, could not be stopped, and
# was listed nowhere until the home page was rewritten.
#
#  - vita/download.c: the active downloads are kept in a list (with a
#    page-unique id and a smoothed rate) and the last 8 ended ones with
#    their result. vita_download_progress() feeds the strip;
#    vita_download_cancel() stops one as the GTK frontend does
#    (download_context_abort + download_context_destroy, the partial file
#    removed); vita_download_page() writes the Downloads page; progress is
#    logged every 500 ms. The start message lasts 2 s instead of the whole
#    download.
#  - vita/main.c: a strip above the HUD (at the bottom with the HUD off):
#    the bar, then name, percent, KiB of KiB, rate and time left.
#  - vita/remote.c: /downloads on the browser's own listener -- like the
#    settings page (241), only to this device: a <progress> bar per active
#    download (drawn since patch 218), a 1 s refresh while anything
#    downloads, Cancel links (/downloads?cancel=ID), the recent results.
#  - vita/chrome.c: the home page links Downloads; the listener's settings
#    and downloads pages are kept out of the history (browser chrome, as
#    Chrome keeps chrome:// pages out).
#  - vita/interact.c: C_DLRECENT -- after the download test, the downloads
#    page opens and its newest entry is vita-test.bin, saved.
#
# Gate: full run-vita-sim.sh exit 0, interaction 52/52 at both speeds
# (step 49 "the downloads page lists it"). The strip and cancel need a
# slow download to be seen: the device checklist (doc 10) covers them.
#
